            <ArticleTitle>Spinal anesthesia for emergency abdominal surgery in uncontrolled hyperthyroidism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with uncontrolled hyperthyroidism presenting as an emergency are at considerable risk. The anesthetic management of a thyrotoxic patient undergoing incidental emergency surgery is discussed. We focus on the intraoperative problems and, above all, postoperative pain management with regional anesthesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
